  (text "4mm banana WHITE input\n+12-16V always-live from track PSU (40-90A source)\nModule draws only ~35mA from this rail via F1 and LDO\nTrack power path (BLACK) bypasses this circuit entirely" (at 15 60 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "LDO power dissipation:\n  12.4V rail: P = (12.4-3.3) x 0.035 = 0.32W, dT = 20C\n  16.0V rail: P = (16.0-3.3) x 0.035 = 0.44W, dT = 27C\nBoth within AMS1117-3.3 125C Tj limit at 25C ambient.\nSolder SOT-223 tab to copper pour for best performance." (at 15 75 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))
  (text "TVS selection note:\nP6KE18CA — bidirectional (CA suffix) is ESSENTIAL.\nUnidirectional P6KE18A only clamps one polarity.\nInductive switching on this rail produces transients\nin both directions." (at 80 75 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left)))


  (text "USB POWER PATH:\nVBUS -> F_USB (500mA polyfuse) -> D_USB (BAT54, SOT-23)\n     -> LDO input node (joins WHITE path after D_WHITE)\n\nD_USB: anode=VBUS_fused, cathode=LDO_input\nD_USB CRITICAL: must be oriented correctly.\nReversed D_USB = track voltage on USB host = HOST DAMAGE.\n\nC_USB1: 10uF 10V MLCC 0805 on VBUS (before F_USB)\nF_USB: 500mA polyfuse 0805\nR_CC1: 5.1k 0402, CC1->GND\nR_CC2: 5.1k 0402, CC2->GND" (at 20 20 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)))

